            <ArticleTitle>Spinal cord compression: an oncologic emergency associated with metastatic cancer: evaluation and management for the home health clinician.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>439-46; quiz 447-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spinal cord compression is an oncologic emergency that needs to be identified, evaluated, and treated promptly for favorable patient outcomes. Although there are nonmalignant types of spinal cord compression, this article focuses on patients presenting with metastatic cancer. Home care clinicians should be knowledgeable with current assessment strategies aimed at recognizing this potentially debilitating condition. Using an assessment tool could assist clinicians with early detection of spinal cord compression, which could improve the overall quality of life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
